<title>ARGENTINA: Banco Frances Q1 EPS rises to $0.15.</title>
<headline>Banco Frances Q1 EPS rises to $0.15.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended Sept 30</p>
<p>Shr $0.15 vs $0.13</p>
<p>ADS $0.44 vs $0.39</p>
<p>Net $18.68 million vs $16.67 million  </p>
<p>Note: The Argentine bank said net financial income rose to $50.5 million from $45.8 million in Q1 1995. It added that charges for unrecoverable debts rose to $15.65 million from $6.64 million.</p>
<p>Net loans outstanding rose to $2.08 billion from $1.64 billion.</p>
<p>-- Gary Regenstreif, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0618</p>
</text>
